  "audio": "022.anthropic-formalized-this.mp3",
  "paragraph": 22,
  "text": "Anthropic formalized this in a clean two-phase pattern for long-running harnesses. First, an initializer agent runs once at the start of a project to create a startup script, a structured JSON feature checklist, a plain-text progress file, and a clean baseline commit. Next, a sequence of fresh coding agent sessions takes over. Each shift reads the state and tackles one scoped item at a time. It reproduces the auth race, adds the lock, verifies concurrency tests, commits clean code, and updates the progress notes for the next shift.",
